<http://data.silknow.org/object/3f5e58ce-4553-3a61-ac64-009b4cc3386c>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "This hanging is one of a set of four that were probably designed to decorate a doorway pilaster. Pilasters are flat columns that formed part of the wooden panelling of an interior.\nThe long rectangular shaft of a pilaster was suited to narrow, vertical decoration, in the form of carvings, or for hangings such as here. Decoration for pilaster hangings typically included stylised floral motifs and scrolling foliage."@en , "Watered silk ground with embroidery mainly in floss (unspun) silk in laid and couched work"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/a7a9aa83-afb5-375a-ae25-d8566025ab4e> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "This hanging is one of a set of four that were probably designed to decorate a doorway pilaster. Pilasters are flat columns that formed part of the wooden panelling of an interior.\nThe long rectangular shaft of a pilaster was suited to narrow, vertical decoration, in the form of carvings, or for hangings such as here. Decoration for pilaster hangings typically included stylised floral motifs and scrolling foliage."@en , "Watered silk ground with embroidery mainly in floss (unspun) silk in laid and couched work"@en ;
